# RSS feeds: OrderBy must start with a letter, so text cut off the signed Query cannot move into it
From bcec66f977efbf933b735023d4c8805cc871eda8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PLD backport <claude.domena@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:00:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Require RSS feed sort fields to start with a letter

The CVE-2026-108278 fix checks that the argument after Query looks like
a sort argument, but with Order empty the OrderBy pattern also accepts a
leading digit. Digits trimmed off the end of a signed Query therefore
still validate: a feed signed for Query "id > 1000", Order "", OrderBy
"Created" is accepted as Query "id > 1", OrderBy "000Created". Today the
database rejects the resulting ORDER BY main.000Created and the feed
comes back empty, so nothing leaks, but the signature check should not
rely on that.

Every RT sort field (core columns, CustomField.{..}, CF.{..}, role and
custom role columns, Custom.Ownership) starts with a letter, so require
that.

PLD hardening beyond upstream: RT 5.0.11 and 6.0.4 carry the same check.

CVE: CVE-2026-108278

diff --git a/share/html/NoAuth/rss/dhandler b/share/html/NoAuth/rss/dhandler
index ba8581fc4..55282c802 100644
--- a/share/html/NoAuth/rss/dhandler
+++ b/share/html/NoAuth/rss/dhandler
@@ -79,7 +79,9 @@ my @search_args = qw(Query Order OrderBy);
 # a sort argument keeps the split where it was signed.
 my %sort_format = (
     Order   => qr{^(?:ASC|DESC)?$}i,
-    OrderBy => qr{^[\w.]*(?:\{[^{}]*\}[\w.]*)*$},
+    # Sort fields start with a letter; digits trimmed off the end of the
+    # Query (e.g. "id > 1000" replayed as "id > 1") must not pass as one
+    OrderBy => qr{^(?:[A-Za-z_][\w.]*(?:\{[^{}]*\}[\w.]*)*)?$},
 );
 
 for my $arg (qw(Order OrderBy)) {
